{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/128285-magnetism-and-the-like","id":128285,"title":"Magnetism and the like...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-08T08:46:30-07:00","id":128285,"title":"Magnetism and the like...","content":"I know this may sound like a weird question, but would Demons in their natural forms be affected by magnetism like machines would? Could you pin one down with a strong enough magnetic field? Would an electromagnetic burst from say an EMP grenade make them shut down?<br /> <br /> Or are Demons other-worldly enough that they wouldn't have to worry about things like that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T10:13:33-07:00","id":128343,"title":"","content":"That's an entertaining thought. As with all these kinds of questions, I'm gonna say it depends on what works in your game's narrative.<br /> <br /> If I were STing a Hunter game and the PCs were trying to find a way to deal with the seemingly unstoppable mechanical horror in the Fire &amp; Smoke Factory (tm) as the real antagonist fled the scene, I'd probably let them get away with shutting a demon down via EMP or capturing it using a convenient super electromagnet. That's the kind of trope that works well in a Hunter game - on par with the tactics for dealing with a Slasher. Also, it lets the PCs do something cool, and the players get to feel smart for coming up with a clever tactic for dealing with a foe they probably couldn't take on in a toe-to-toe fight. Besides which, if they start stockpiling EMP grenades so they can shut down demons whenever they want, I can always send in non-demon antagonists their way to make sure it doesn't render all the baddies helpless against the hunters.<br /> <br /> In a Demon game I'd be more cautious. First, if an NPC wrecks the PCs' day using magnets or EMP grenades, it's gonna feel a little cheap, and I might get some pushback and arguments that metal doesn't necessarily mean ferrous metal, my character's form is organic, etc. Second, once that Pandora's box is open, I can't close it. Demons will always be an important feature of the game, and if I make EMP/magnets a highly effective against Unchained in their demonic form those weapons will quickly become standard equipment for anyone who might have to fight demons (and hey, my group might be totally okay with that, but I need to bear that in mind before I make the decision).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T10:25:50-07:00","id":128351,"title":"","content":"I would say a weakness towards magnetics or fields would make for a good glitch, but otherwise I wouldn't penalize a demon player for having non-organic vs organic form components. As a glitch, the weakness has in game justification, and also makes their human form itself more interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T14:16:58-07:00","id":128515,"title":"","content":"And don't forget that there's an EMP Field form power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thread Reaper <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">\uff1c(\u00b4 \u055e)\u0a0a( \u055e )\uff1e\ufeff</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/377-xanandithras","name":"Xanandithras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar377_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T08:31:06-07:00","id":129910,"title":"","content":"If EMPs would be destroying the angels, then the electricity based powers would also be doing more damage. <br /> <br /> As this is clearly not the case, I think that we're going to have to say that no, they're not electronic-based machines which would be affected by magnetic fields.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T14:00:40-07:00","id":130149,"title":"","content":"Here is a Thought linked to mcn's point. They are fueled by essance not electricity so emp could affect them like it would a ghost-oblivious to it. they are not machines as we can build or fully understand so there is no reason we could be certain it would affect them. <br /> <br /> let us say you do try this. The angel sees you activate it and goes wide eyed then falls to the ground. When you do the clique 'poke it with a stick' it jumps to action. It knows a humans curiosity would 90% of the time keep it from running and it only desires to accomplish it's mission. Angels don't care about using dirty tricks. So my advise? If your st does have it be affected pump it full of lead.<br /> <br /> Even if he doesn't do the above trickery you have to wonder how long before it reboots or worse...it has been disconnected from the machine. More are on their way and like the Borg the machine adapts. these angels would have counter measures but to give all these measures would be inefficient. The efficient action is to ensure you never share discovery","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T22:08:28-07:00","id":131609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/128285-magnetism-and-the-like?p=128343#post128343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides which, if they start stockpiling EMP grenades so they can shut down demons whenever they want, I can always send in non-demon antagonists their way to make sure it doesn't render all the baddies helpless against the hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or just Demons whose bodies are organic, and that's why they were chosen to do things.<br /> <br /> But overall, I like your thinking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":1642,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","user":"Paddon","date":". 05-11-2014, 01:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}